    "update_time": null,
    "content": {
     "content_type": "text",
     "parts": [
      "> I'm writing to appeal citation #[number] issued on [date] at 7:58 PM in the Perry Street lot.\n>\n> The posted sign at the lot entrance [describe location] reads \"Permit Required 7 AM – 5 PM.\" Relying on that sign, I parked after 5 PM believing the lot was open. The citation states enforcement until 8 PM. I've attached a photo of the sign taken [date/time].\n>\n> Since the posted hours don't match the enforcement hours on the citation, I respectfully request that the citation be voided. If the enforcement hours for this lot differ from the signage, I'd also suggest updating the sign so others aren't caught by the same discrepancy.\n>\n> Thank you for your consideration,\n> David Barron\n\nTake a clear photo of the exact sign (with the lot visible) before you submit. That photo is what wins these."
     ]
    },
